  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile aggregation is the dominant performance lever (~13% gain over singleprofile), and the current best configurations (config_005/006) use scVI_n200 in the RNA-only multiprofile setting (~0.650-0.653). We have tested PCA and scVI as RNA encoders but have never evaluated scGPT, leaving a critical gap in the encoder landscape. Question: config_008 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scGPT, avgpool) is a clean single-variable swap from config_005 (scVI→scGPT), directly testing whether a different learned encoder captures complementary gene-expression structure that scVI misses in the highest-impact setting. Why best next: Under a limited budget, resolving whether encoder choice beyond scVI matters in the multiprofile regime is the highest-information experiment—if scGPT substantially outperforms scVI, it redefines the search ceiling and justifies further encoder exploration; if it is comparable, it confirms scVI is near-optimal and redirects effort toward fusion/multimodal questions. This avoids the risk of testing a second variable (e.g., fusion strategy) while the encoder dimension remains unexplored in the setting that produces the best results."
}

